<section class="mn-section mn-intro" aria-label="About">
  <p>Hi! I’m Wenhao, a 17 year old from NJ. I am currently working on <strong>human-centric AI</strong> through AI safety research and teaching people to build AI responsibly.</p>
  <p>
    I founded <a href="https://nxthorizon.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NXT Horizon</a>, an <strong>AI incubator for underrepresented students</strong> with 128 chapters and 560+ AI projects built by our students. Through NXT, I <strong>mentored students to the NeurIPS main conference</strong> (Creative AI Track).
    I also co-founded <a href="https://yimo-official.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YIMO</a>, a math competition that grew to 3,700+ competitors in 8 months.
  </p>
  <p>
    I’ve worked as a software engineering intern at <a href="https://www.venu3d.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Venu AI (YC W21)</a> and have conducted math and AI research at Stevens Institute of Technology, where I <strong>received a grant from Google DeepMind</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>Outside of that, I enjoy playing baseball and writing poetry. I’m a huge fan of Emily Dickinson, <em>The Mentalist</em>, the Red Sox, <a href="https://www.uniqlo.com/us/en/news/topics/2025092601/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Labubu T-shirts</a>, and collecting baseball cards.</p>
</section>

